WEBVTT

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:06.730
Yotaka!

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.620
Yotaka!

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.470
Yogi, stand back.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.680
Yogi, stand back.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.710
Wings of Morning Light
Score 6

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.560
What a miserable sight you are.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.650
Such sloppy work, and letting your blood  be spilled.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.190
You are the disgrace of Circus.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.070
Kiichi.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.440
Why is someone from the First Ship here...

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.450
Just because the enemy was an acquaintance of someone you know,

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.200
you hesitated to put him to rest and instead had the tables turned on you.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.620
You're so soft that it makes me sick.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.380
How long have you been here?

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:03.010
Having someone like you share the same rank as an elite like me, Kiichi, is so annoying.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.560
Oh, good job being a decoy.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.920
Yotaka...

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.720
<i>Yogi is hurt.</i>

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.690
<i>Tsubame-chan is crying.</i>

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.900
Gareki-kun, well…

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.950
You look badly hurt.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.410
Are you okay?

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.870
Yeah, thanks for asking.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.670
<i>Gareki isn't hurt badly.</i>

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:23.970
<i>He's not crying, but I think he's just holding it back.</i>

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:31.390
<i>I'm not hurt either, yet I feel a tightness in my chest.</i>

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.890
<i>It's like feeling sad...</i>

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.270
<i>Why do I feel this way?</i>

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:39.190
<i>And when I think of that man, I feel sick.</i>

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:46.570
<i>I get a cold feeling right here and it hurts.</i>

00:05:54.870 --> 00:06:01.040
A coward who never comes out to act in
person but enjoys tormenting the weak,

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.590
as noted on the First Ship's wanted list.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:11.050
When your pet grew unexpectedly strong and hurt Yogi,

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:15.060
did you get carried away and miss the chance to escape?

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.020
It’s fun to torment others, isn't it?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:22.730
Go!

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.650
Your girls are great.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.530
You control them well.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.240
Capture completed, huh?

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:19.290
I deeply appreciate your cooperation, Second Ship Captain, Hirato-dono.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.080
You're so full of nonsense.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:23.630
Return.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.470
That's so unkind, I was just thanking you.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.100
That's so unkind, I was just thanking you.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:56.240
Yogi-san, are you with
that person who killed Yotaka?

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.120
Yeah.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:04.040
Wait, Tsubame, they are members of Circus.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:06.540
Circus?

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.210
You know about Circus, don’t you?

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.800
The elite group of people who hunt down criminals.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.180
I happened to get involved with these people,

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.470
and learned that there are monsters called Varuga.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:26.150
They killed Tsubaki and turned Yotaka into that.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:29.690
Gareki-kun, I will tell her the rest.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:39.330
The organization that’s creating Varuga
is called Kafka by the government.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.200
There are two distinct kinds of Varuga.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:45.620
One kind is created by Kafka
itself by repeated cell fusion.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:52.840
And the other kind transforms due to damage to their
cells caused by Varuga blood or body fluid.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.680
They're originally victims, just like Yotaka-kun.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:05.230
The drug Yotaka-kun was forced to take was
probably implanted with Varuga cells.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:07.860
The drug.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:12.400
Varuga have an extremely fast cell renewal cycle.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.570
Even if they get badly hurt, they'll recover in a few days.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.290
In order to support that rapid metabolic system,

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.540
they devour others and integrate the cells of their victims into themselves.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:32.800
Circus' mission is to eliminate all Varugas,
put them to rest, and to annihilate Kafka.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.840
Our role is to end the lives of those...

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.180
who were made to undergo twisted
evolution based on the desires of others,

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.310
and set them free from all their chains.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:50.610
I'm sorry. "Set them free" is too nice a way to say it.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.190
That's what we were told,

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.320
but in the end,

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.950
we're just killing people who turned into Varuga...

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.830
because we can't return them to how they were before.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.750
Then...

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:08.290
kill me.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.170
You...

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.630
Kill me too.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:16.800
What are you talking about!

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:21.890
You're not a Varuga!

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:31.440
I was taking that drug for a while too.

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:36.570
I may transform some day.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.570
Tsubame-chan.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:48.040
Also, Yotaka isn't here anymore!

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.170
I don’t want to be alone.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.380
I don't like that. I'm scared of being alone.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:54.800
I don't like that. I'm scared of being alone.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:11:01.050
Tsubaki-oneechan died, and Grandpa who
was in the hospital forgot all about me.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.680
And now, Yotaka has died too.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.810
Even so, your grandfather is still alive!

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:12.190
Didn't the two of you work really hard in order to pay the hospital fees?!

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.690
The money we earned wasn't nearly enough.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:23.280
But apparently, Grandpa's old friend had been paying part of the fees.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.700
That's what the nurse secretly told me.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:30.000
So he'll be fine even if I'm gone.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.210
I just want to disappear...

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.130
Tsubame...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:43.720
<i>Tsubame-chan is crying.</i>

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.720
<i>Drip, drop.</i>

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.770
<i>It's almost as if she's sinking.</i>

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:02.110
Kii-chan, did you find anything over there?

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:07.280
There are lots of research materials,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.830
but nothing indicates his connection with Kafka.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.420
Sheesh, they really have their bases covered.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.960
I didn't think they would leave any evidence from the beginning.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:23.220
But I can't help but admire them for the extreme care they take.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.640
Even if they're the enemy,
I cannot help but praise them.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.970
Jiki-kun, what are you thinking, admiring the enemy?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:36.110
Well, the only thing left to do
is to ask him directly, isn't it?

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:42.740
What a sorry sight you are.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.820
You sound just like Akari-chan.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.450
That's not the way you should address
someone who's 6 years older than you.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:50.700
Show him respect and call him "sensei."

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.580
Okay, okay.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:58.790
Oh right, speaking of Akari-sensei, he found
an interesting notebook in the Niji Forest.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.380
Let’s have a tea party with the three of us to discuss that notebook.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.340
Your "tea" means alcohol, doesn't it?

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.140
Of course.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.890
Akari-san won’t come if I'm around.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:13.850
Hey, you didn't address him as "sensei" either!

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.560
I'm an exception, because he doesn't like me.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.190
That's not the point.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.860
Please finish the job in front of you.

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.610
Have you been fooling around all this time?

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:25.400
Darn it.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.030
I know, I know.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.620
So did you find anything?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.740
Nothing at all.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:35.120
That's why we thought that there's no other way
except to ask this creature here directly.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.790
Although, I don't think he'll answer our questions willingly.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.880
Let's try asking anyway.

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:46.380
I'll give you a chance to atone for your sins.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:49.930
Tell me everything about what you aimed to achieve with your actions,

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:52.640
and how you're related to Kafka.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.890
Were you the one who distributed the drug?

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:57.640
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.110
What?

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.440
Foolish humans like you...

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:05.990
Eh?

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:11.200
Tell me about your relationship with Palnedo.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.260
Hirato and the others are putting him to rest.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.340
They've defeated that man.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.010
<i>He's dead...</i>

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.140
<i>The man who caused the deaths of Tsubaki and Yotaka is dead.</i>

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:43.860
<i>This should've been what I had strongly wished for.</i>

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:46.400
<i>And yet...</i>

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.700
<i>Gareki's heart is feeling the same as me.</i>

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.540
<i>A feeling of tightness...</i>

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.120
<i>I wonder if the reason I can't put my feelings to rest is because...</i>

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:02.670
<i>I didn't get to kill him with my own hands...</i>

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.760
Meiga has been wiped out by them.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:09.970
Meiga?

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:21.940
Who's that?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.200
That boy...

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.570
Are you talking about Nai?

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.910
No, I'm talking about Gareki.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.450
He was on that ship, right?

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:41.870
The ship that we sank back then.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.630
I guess everything is predestined by fate, huh?

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:57.810
Well, I don't know.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:05.520
Hirato-san.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:07.570
You look like there's something you want to say, Yogi.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:08.690
You look like there's something you want to say, Yogi.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:15.320
Back in the Niji Forest, Gareki was attacked by the bestial Varuga,

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.990
and yet he was unhurt.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:20.830
From this, we deduced that they wanted to abduct him,

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.580
so we used him as bait.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.550
The members from the First Ship were originally
in charge of the events that occurred here,

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:30.550
but you said you were coming here.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:34.840
So you were partly here as a loan to the First Ship
members in order to attract the attention of that coward.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:39.010
Also, if the ones who attacked Gareki appeared as well,
we would be killing two birds with one stone.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.310
I'm sorry, Gareki-kun.

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:46.610
About what? That's part of your job, isn't it?

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.240
Damn it!

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.450
Well now,

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:01.370
may I ask you to come along with us?

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:02.870
Hold on!

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:05.500
What are you–

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:11.050
Tsubame...

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:15.380
Why are you going with them?

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.850
You're not alone, right?

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:19.890
Grandpa's still...

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:23.770
You'll still have people around–

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:24.770
Even you, Gareki...

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.320
Even you left me and went somewhere far away.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:37.530
There's no one who remains by my side any more.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:45.210
Why did you leave us?

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:54.300
We felt so lonely at home after you disappeared...

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:15.320
Well then, I'll be waiting here.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.740
Just take your time to talk.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:20.990
Yes, sir. Thank you for being so considerate.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:26.330
I don't believe it! Someone from Circus?

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.330
He's so cool, isn't he?
He's so cool!

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:36.590
Grandpa.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:39.590
It's Tsubame.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:44.680
Grandpa, I've decided to leave the village.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:48.390
I think it's possible I won't be able to come here again.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:50.600
But, don't worry,

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:56.530
because the people of Circus will be taking good care of you.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.660
Grandpa, please live to a ripe old age, okay?

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.700
I wonder who the old man in this ward is,

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.500
to have Circus come here for his sake?

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.620
Even the young man who paid his
hospital fees is such a mystery.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.920
Which young man?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.380
He also came by here yesterday, remember?

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:16.090
I think he's still in his teens.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.130
He has black hair, and looks really dashing!

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.970
Oh, that young man–

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.140
Excuse me!

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.390
What's his name?!

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.390
Please tell me!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:35.320
Now that you mention it, when your grandfather was still conscious,

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:36.900
I heard him calling the man "Gareki"...

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:43.320
<i>Welcome home!</i>

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.740
<i>Huh? Where's Gareki?</i>

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:53.460
<i>I think Gareki is hanging out with bad
company and doing dangerous stuff.</i>

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:54.710
<i>What?</i>

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.750
<i>Forget about him.</i>

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.670
<i>He's a complete stranger to us now.</i>

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.020
Gareki!

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:17.190
Are you finished with your business in Karasuna?

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:19.690
I could've settled everything for you if you had just told me...

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:21.570
that you were going to renew the lease for this land.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.700
Are you trying to safeguard the grave of your family?

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.370
I have no family.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:41.010
The reason why you left them was because
you didn't want to implicate them, isn't it?

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:45.340
What an adorable thing to do.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:47.550
Shut up.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.560
<i>I was protected by so many people.</i>

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:56.560
<i>They gave me so much encouragement.</i>

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:59.320
Are you finished with your visit?

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.240
I have a request.

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:10.200
<i>With the remaining time left of my life...</i>

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:14.080
I don't mind even if you have
to hurt me or cut me up,

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.330
I'm willing to...

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.880
I'm willing to offer my body as
a specimen in order to defeat Kafka!

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:22.840
<i>I swear I'll not live a meaningless life.</i>

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.260
Please make use of my body!

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.850
What a wonderful look.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.860
<i>Until the day my life comes to an end...</i>

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:40.190
I'll gladly accept a gem like you.

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:53.290
<i>I'll put you, who couldn't fly, onto my wings and we'll fly together!</i>

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:30.630
Akari-san, if you're so irritable, it'll have an adverse effect on your work.

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:32.640
If you know that, then get out of my sight now.

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:37.100
What a thing to say. To think that all along
I've had such a calming effect on you...

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:38.930
Stop disturbing me! Get out!
